# contacts' never-contact routes (core/modules/contacts/README.md "Routes"): a member's session,
# suppression.read for the list, suppression.write to add or remove an entry. POST is @Idempotent():
# the Idempotency-Key is an example UUID; another one adds again, and an active entry with the same
# key is answered unchanged. A write sends the cookie, so it sends Origin: {{appOrigin}} too.
# `suppressionId` is an entry of your workspace, from the list: put it in
# http-client.private.env.json.

### GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/contacts/suppression: the active entries and opt-outs, newest first, a page at a time, each with the person or company of the workspace it names
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/contacts/suppression?limit=50
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### POST /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/contacts/suppression: adds an entry, here a company by its domain (or a person by personId or a profile URL, a company by companyId or its page; layer opt_out for a person's opt-out by hand); 201 with the entry; 400 suppression_target_invalid for a value that normalizes to nothing, a single-label domain or a company with neither domain nor page; 404 person_not_found, company_not_found
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/contacts/suppression
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}
Idempotency-Key: 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000002010

{ "kind": "company", "value": "competitor.example" }

### DELETE /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/contacts/suppression/{id}: removes a never-contact entry, kept on record with its removal; 204; 409 suppression_not_removable for an opt-out; 404 suppression_not_found
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/contacts/suppression/{{suppressionId}}
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}
